      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e2",
      "title": "il fait + a weather word",
      "body": "• For weather, use il fait + adjective: Il fait froid; il fait beau.\n• Use il y a + noun for another common pattern: Il y a du vent; il y a de la neige (review from Unit 10).\n• You may also hear the set phrases il pleut (it is raining) and il neige (it is snowing)."
    },
